{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus","id":1019815,"title":"What Happens if No Lupus","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-20T09:26:34-08:00","id":1019815,"title":"What Happens if No Lupus","content":"I'm a fan of Forsaken, but one of my players is an Apocalypse only guy. If I were to accommodate him, the one thing that I really can't get down with is Lupus characters (which is probably why I'm a Forsaken guy). How much of the system/lore breaks if I just get rid of lupus, and make it a thing that doesn't exist or no longer exists? Note that this is just a weird personal preference thing. I'm sure everyone else loves Lupus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T09:35:11-08:00","id":1019821,"title":"","content":"No, not everyone loves Lupus, but I digress.<br /> <br /> The Lupus affects the game in two major ways, aside being a character option: the great interest on the Garou Nation's part to keep them existing, and the Red Talon's Tribe, that is Lupus Only (and the main source of Lupus Garou).<br /> <br /> For your game, the easiest way to get rid of Lupus changing the least in the game would be for the Talon's totems falling to the Wyrm so awesomely that they curse all Lupus to loose the Change if they don't go for the Wyrm. With Lupus being rare and wolves dying in the setting, that wouldn't be so unbelievable at the doors of the Apocalypse. The Nation mourns the lost of the Breed and the Talon's Tribe, and that's it. The setting takes on a even more accentuated fall to the Apocalypse, but remains mostly intact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T10:01:15-08:00","id":1019828,"title":"","content":"I think if you take the setting in broad strokes, you can keep it more or less completely intact without the Lupus breed. In modern nights, in setting, Lupus only account for 12-14% (depending on book) of the Garou population.<br /> <br /> What to do with the Talons comes to mind as an initial question. You could just write them out and pretend they never existed. You could have them be a Metis Tribe. Sort of an alternative to the Spirals that isn't completely corrupt but still hates Homids and &quot;adopts&quot; the unwanted (Metis) from other Tribes. Griffin could stay in place with little rewriting.<br /> <br /> You might want to boost starting Gnosis by 1, if you're going to eliminate Lupus. But that's more a mechanical idea than an in story one.<br /> <br /> All in all, I think it is completely doable without breaking the setting.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T10:25:55-08:00","id":1019837,"title":"","content":"Or you could just do what some of my friends do and just ban Lupus characters because they are incapable of dealing with human society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T10:55:33-08:00","id":1019852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1019837#post1019837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you could just do what some of my friends do and just ban Lupus characters because they are incapable of dealing with human society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I've been in games where Lupus characters were banned, though more because most human players don't know how to role play Lupus. You can even not have Lupus NPCs. With the Lupus numbers being so low, it is totally possible that a Garou would never met a Lupus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 12-20-2016, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T11:19:17-08:00","id":1019866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1019837#post1019837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> because they are incapable of dealing with human society.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the reasoning behind this statement?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T11:44:22-08:00","id":1019875,"title":"","content":"Question for the OP, what is your issue with Lupus? And what makes metis different from lupus so you can tolerate them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T11:56:00-08:00","id":1019886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus#post1019815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a fan of Forsaken, but one of my players is an Apocalypse only guy. If I were to accommodate him, the one thing that I really can't get down with is Lupus characters (which is probably why I'm a Forsaken guy). How much of the system/lore breaks if I just get rid of lupus, and make it a thing that doesn't exist or no longer exists? Note that this is just a weird personal preference thing. I'm sure everyone else loves Lupus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's a large chunk of lore centered on the phrase losing the wolf. On a personal level, it means that you've lost a measure of ferocity and wildness, mechanically defined by dropping to 0 temporary Rage and Willpower, and the individual in question can no longer shapeshift or regain Rage until they regain Willpower. Occasionally, more extreme needs for recovery crop up, such as with Vic Stryker, who lost the wolf for decades before becoming able to shapeshift again.<br /> <br /> In a wider, more group-related sense, it means something way more serious, because the werebeast cannot exist without the beast. The Apis are pretty much gone for good because all wild aurochs are gone; recovering the changer would mean somehow recovering the aurochs or a spiritually-compatible equivalent in some fashion. The same would happen to the Garou if all wild wolves died.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">No, not everyone loves Lupus, but I digress.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Lupus affects the game in two major ways, aside being a character option: the great interest on the Garou Nation's part to keep them existing, and the Red Talon's Tribe, that is Lupus Only (and the main source of Lupus Garou).</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Red Talons are not at all the main source of lupus Garou; that would be every tribe other than the Walkers and Gnawers. The Talons number only 500 or so, at most, and the Garou Nation consists of over ten thousand Garou, about in in seven of whom are born of wolf. Thus, all other tribes would consist of 2/3 or more of wolf-born Garou.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">For your game, the easiest way to get rid of Lupus changing the least in the game would be for the Talon's totems falling to the Wyrm so awesomely that they curse all Lupus to loose the Change if they don't go for the Wyrm. With Lupus being rare and wolves dying in the setting, that wouldn't be so unbelievable at the doors of the Apocalypse. The Nation mourns the lost of the Breed and the Talon's Tribe, and that's it. The setting takes on a even more accentuated fall to the Apocalypse, but remains mostly intact.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> As noted, that would mean that the Garou ceased to exist entirely before any great apocalyptic battle even happened. Also, it relies on the aforementioned faulty assumption about lupus distribution, as well as being out of character for Griffin and his brood. They would die before giving in, and hence, die they probably will.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T11:59:19-08:00","id":1019887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1019852#post1019852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. I've been in games where Lupus characters were banned, though more because most human players don't know how to role play Lupus. You can even not have Lupus NPCs. With the Lupus numbers being so low, it is totally possible that a Garou would never met a Lupus.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is one of the reasons, it is hard to understand animals without serious reflection. Try walking on all fours and eating without your hands for a meal or two, and you will start to understand that they have to have different assumptions than humans just based on differences in manual dexterity and posture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T12:03:30-08:00","id":1019890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1019887#post1019887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is one of the reasons, it is hard to understand animals without serious reflection. Try walking on all fours and eating without your hands for a meal or two, and you will start to understand that they have to have different assumptions than humans just based on differences in manual dexterity and posture.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lupus are also human, though, as much as homid are wolf. They can learn how to use hands pretty fast, just like homids can learn how to walk and run on all fours, move their ears and tail and such.<br /> <br /> Honestly, with lupus, just read an article or two that is up to date about wolf behaviour. As in, no alpha or omega used for social structure. It needs to be no more difficult than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T12:19:21-08:00","id":1019901,"title":"","content":"W20 ended a rather important lupus problem of not speaking a human language without Linguistics, too, just as it ended Linguistics and replaced it with Academics. Lupus still get one (human) language for free, so that's one major hurdle of old out of the way. It's less a matter of having no idea about what to do and playing someone who's at times uncomfortable and tends not to see human people in the same light they see themselves, albeit way farther off than just coming from another human culture. They'll be taken aback at how humans blithely move about without any concern for potential threats, feel the need to move around more often, and also, the concept of grocery stores will make them uneasy, but they'll ultimately be better able to adjust to life among normal humans than <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MRQBp-CYYLk\" target=\"_blank\">a certain anime character</a>. Also, they won't punctuate their sentences quite so strangely as another, similar character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T12:34:57-08:00","id":1019910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1019890#post1019890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Lupus are also human, though, as much as homid are wolf. They can learn how to use hands pretty fast, just like homids can learn how to walk and run on all fours, move their ears and tail and such.<br /> <br /> Honestly, with lupus, just read an article or two that is up to date about wolf behaviour. As in, no alpha or omega used for social structure. It needs to be no more difficult than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>So much this.<br /> <br /> By the time a Lupus character has gone through their Rite of Passage, the manual dexterity issues should have already been learned. Their foundational outlook is going to be a bit different, but that's the interesting part of the Breed to me.<br /> <br /> It's worth restating. Lupus are as human as Homids are wolf.<br /> <br /> By a few Ranks in, the outlook gap is going to be smaller too. Lupus are in no way &quot;incapable of dealing with human society.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1019901#post1019901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W20 ended a rather important lupus problem of not speaking a human language without Linguistics, too, just as it ended Linguistics and replaced it with Academics. Lupus still get one (human) language for free, so that's one major hurdle of old out of the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had actually always assumed Lupus got the local human language for free. I hadn't realized that that was a house rule.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T13:07:45-08:00","id":1019940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1019901#post1019901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W20 ended a rather important lupus problem of not speaking a human language without Linguistics, too, just as it ended Linguistics and replaced it with Academics. Lupus still get one (human) language for free, so that's one major hurdle of old out of the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes Lupus much more playable. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T14:05:10-08:00","id":1019959,"title":"","content":"Wow, thanks for all the advice. The whole idea of a person going into an animal form and sexing up animals weirds me out. Also, it's weird to me that Lupus can function at all and don't have all their Intelligence-type attributes and skills capped at 1 die. Again, just a preference thing. I'm trying to find out a way to accommodate this guy without having to mess with Lupus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T14:10:41-08:00","id":1019961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1019959#post1019959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, thanks for all the advice. The whole idea of a person going into an animal form and sexing up animals weirds me out. Also, it's weird to me that Lupus can function at all and don't have all their Intelligence-type attributes and skills capped at 1 die. Again, just a preference thing. I'm trying to find out a way to accommodate this guy without having to mess with Lupus.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lupus Garou are human level smart wolves. If you teach a Lupus and he is willing, he will learn.<br /> <br /> For most Garou, the human animal divide is blurred. Wolves are people to Garou. Humans are just a different type of animal, an animal that is throwing the world out of balance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T14:15:27-08:00","id":1019964,"title":"","content":"<i>Comment removed as it was of quesationable taste.</i><br /> <br /> you can keep a lot, but take heed its one of the essential divides between forsaken and apocalypse... Why I never touched forsaken once.<br /> <br /> there your cursed, in apocalypse your blessed.<br /> <br /> Forsaken (as some I cant remember who, have said to the point of annoyance) is a game that &quot;Gives your chars more room to create unique goals , because it doesnt <i>assign</i> you an ovveriding goal like apoacalypse does&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Chronicles of darkness is pretty big on this whole &quot;All supernaturals used to be ordinary humans&quot; thing, withh the exception of prometheans, who seek to <i>become</i> ordinary humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":".  Removed a comment of questionable taste. 12-20-2016, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T14:30:31-08:00","id":1019973,"title":"","content":"Even the Ground admit that not all humans are throwing everything out of wack. Hunter-gather and other traditional groups that manage their population growth are fine, it is everyone else that is the problem. Heck, if the entire world had only grown in population as much as Europe since 1900 (+80%), the global population would be less than 3 billion instead of 7.5 billion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T15:01:19-08:00","id":1019992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1019959#post1019959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, thanks for all the advice. The whole idea of a person going into an animal form and sexing up animals weirds me out. Also, it's weird to me that Lupus can function at all and don't have all their Intelligence-type attributes and skills capped at 1 die. Again, just a preference thing. I'm trying to find out a way to accommodate this guy without having to mess with Lupus.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the cross Breed bredding thing is weird to you, just don't play with it. Have Homids only able to breed with human kinfolk and Lupus with wolf kinfolk. I'm sure that would throw some of the numbers off if you look deep enough into it, but on the surface it would function fine for game I think.<br /> <br /> I think that that would put a deeper divide between the Homid and Lupus Breed Garou, but that could work in your setting variation's favor.<br /> <br /> And as was stated by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3950_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3950\" data-vbnamecard=\"3950\">wonderandawe</a>, Lupus are human level smart. Once Garou go through their first change they come into full human intellect.<br /> <br /> For your player, I don't actually understand the initial issue. If you don't want them to play Lupus, it is easy enough to add that restriction without altering the WtA setting at all. I've run more than one game with such restrictions. Especially for newer players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T15:02:04-08:00","id":1019993,"title":"","content":"yea, I think it's just my chronicle perspective on supernaturals being &quot;used to be human.&quot; As you've all pointed out Lupus aren't wolves at all. They're a gagillion times smarter than wolves, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T15:06:03-08:00","id":1019995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1019993#post1019993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yea, I think it's just my chronicle perspective on supernaturals being &quot;used to be human.&quot; As you've all pointed out Lupus aren't wolves at all. They're a gagillion times smarter than wolves, right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They are as much wolves as homid Garou are human. They are just REALLY smart wolves that can turn into Humans and Wolfman. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T15:14:26-08:00","id":1019999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1019993#post1019993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yea, I think it's just my chronicle perspective on supernaturals being &quot;used to be human.&quot; As you've all pointed out Lupus aren't wolves at all. They're a gagillion times smarter than wolves, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>What about Promethean unfleshed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T15:36:44-08:00","id":1020010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1019973#post1019973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the Ground admit that not all humans are throwing everything out of wack. Hunter-gather and other traditional groups that manage their population growth are fine, it is everyone else that is the problem. Heck, if the entire world had only grown in population as much as Europe since 1900 (+80%), the global population would be less than 3 billion instead of 7.5 billion.</div> </div> </div> </div>There aren't many hunter-gatherers left, given how history went. The zoonotic diseases and greater numbers of agricultural cultures meant that a lot died out after the advent of farming, and those who were left got hit again with smallpox. Nowadays, those people, living in a manner which the Garou might approve? If they lived and the rest died, there'd probably be way less than three billion left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T17:45:34-08:00","id":1020078,"title":"","content":"I think that the Garou (and the Fera in general) would be much happier with 3 billion people than 7.5 billion people (though they would probably still complain about there being too many people). Of course, Kindred and KJ would be unhappy because of the lack of food.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T18:25:16-08:00","id":1020095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1019901#post1019901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W20 ended a rather important lupus problem of not speaking a human language without Linguistics</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1019910#post1019910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had actually always assumed Lupus got the local human language for free. I hadn't realized that that was a house rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>I normally ignore things that I think are wrong that are off-topic-ish, but since this got brought up again, I'm going to have to say &quot;[Citation Needed]&quot;. The description of Lupus character restrictions in W20 is virtually identical to that of WTA First Edition, and Ways of the Wolf makes no mention of Lupus characters not being able to speak Human Tongues without spending points on Linguistics. IME, all Garou that are built through the standard character creation rules understand Lupus Communication, the Garou Tongue, and the lingua franca, regardless of breed. AFAICT, the same justification to force Lupus characters to buy a human language applies to the Homids and Metis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":707,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","user":"etherial","date":". 12-20-2016, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T19:44:58-08:00","id":1020133,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a>, one of the pre-made characters I liked the most is a Wendigo Lupus who actually got a degree and a job at a library even before learning about the Garou society. It is hard on them, but Lupus can and do learn to deal with humans. PCs, on the other hand, usually don't do it very well even when they're Homid, what to say of Lupus...<br /> <br /> Not that I think that White Wolf got right into how the Lupus thing, though, considering the Talons. They're pretty much a tribe of PCs!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar805_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"805\" data-vbnamecard=\"805\">idpersona</a>, I think getting rid retroactively from Lupus would harm the setting just a little because it is mostly what justifies a lot of how Garou society developed. There would never be so much rage on humanity, and probably not any Impergium, if humans were the only reproduction option. A lot of the setting relies on a romanticized view of the Lupus and wolves in general.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a>, interesting numbers, and I'm curious to know the source. Not that I don't believe, just sincerely curious. That said, it doesn't change anything else. All that you said is true, in the sense that it is the most accepted theory in lore to explain the end of the Apis. For one, it doesn't have to apply, because the Apis died for real before their animal Kin died, the Garou are still alive in this scenario. Two, the wolves didn't died, just are in the verge of (and that is in the lore already, no change), so nothing guarantees that the Lupus breed is a necessity. Three, it can be wrong, as far as anyone truly knows, since other things happened that could explain the end of the Apis. No Changing Breed, after all, that went total extinction in the past, recovered, Kin or no Kin. Four, and more important, the OP wants the best way to get rid of the Lupus 'cause he doesn't like Lupus, changing the lore to accommodate for this is already a thing, there is no point in saying he's wrong and harming the lore. The lore isn't sacred, or unchangeable reality, y'now? Its just fiction.<br /> <br /> Oh, and since they have alone a third of the Lupus, the Talons remain as the single main source of Lupus compared to any other tribe. &quot;Main&quot; doesn't mean &quot;responsible for more than half&quot;.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5685_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5685\" data-vbnamecard=\"5685\">Archivist</a>, non-surprisingly, most Homid Garou <u>do</u> agree with you. That's one of the in-setting reasons for so few Lupus. They're born humans, so even they not <u>being</u> more human than they are wolf, they still grew up finding humans, not wolves, attractive. Well, except for that tiny numbers who would find wolves attractive even if they were humans...<br /> <br /> But yeah, Lupus aren't as smart as wolves. Actually, a Lupus is far easier to notice before the Change precisely because of that. They are at human-level intellect, or near to it, since birth (of course, first at child-level int). They don't have the resources to learn much of humanity's knowledge until the Change, but they are still as smart. And they learn lightning fast in the first years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T20:01:57-08:00","id":1020139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1020095#post1020095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I normally ignore things that I think are wrong that are off-topic-ish, but since this got brought up again, I'm going to have to say &quot;[Citation Needed]&quot;. The description of Lupus character restrictions in W20 is virtually identical to that of WTA First Edition, and Ways of the Wolf makes no mention of Lupus characters not being able to speak Human Tongues without spending points on Linguistics. IME, all Garou that are built through the standard character creation rules understand Lupus Communication, the Garou Tongue, and the lingua franca, regardless of breed. AFAICT, the same justification to force Lupus characters to buy a human language applies to the Homids and Metis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell that to many, many STs who, without the W20 blurb on lupus learning languages and human skills, assumed that lupus had to buy languages at creation to speak at all. Or outright banned languages from lupus due to them being feral children. Hence why in W20 blog I pleaded for the lupus desc to have a section like this;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> W20 p.76</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lupus are quite capable of abstract thought, but much<br /> of their experience with the concepts governed by such<br /> thought comes after the First Change. They pick up the<br /> basics of Garou speech very quickly, and the basics of<br /> human languages with surprising speed</div> </div> </div> </div>That would basically say that lupus ARE allowed to speak human languages clearly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T20:31:08-08:00","id":1020150,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar110_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"110\" data-vbnamecard=\"110\">Ana Mizuki</a>, even it was necessary to actually talk aloud that Lupus know languages, it doesn't mean that they previously didn't by the rules. No rule ever said that, and doesn't matter how many STs did it, it was a house rule. There are lots of house-rules in RPGs that are created by use and so many people start to use that few ever see that it is a house-rule. But it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T20:44:18-08:00","id":1020154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1020150#post1020150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar110_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"110\" data-vbnamecard=\"110\">Ana Mizuki</a>, even it was necessary to actually talk aloud that Lupus know languages, it doesn't mean that they previously didn't by the rules. No rule ever said that, and doesn't matter how many STs did it, it was a house rule. There are lots of house-rules in RPGs that are created by use and so many people start to use that few ever see that it is a house-rule. But it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said it wasn't a houserule. But without the books outright stating that lupus can learn languages, getting a ST to LET you have english for free was like pulling teeth. And I cannot stress how freaking common this was. There were articles all over the net how lupus were not supposed to be able to use human languages, as well.<br /> <br /> Yes it was a houserule, but it was similar to the Sleep=shift to breedform one, it was all but accepted as canon in some circles. And since the books did not have a section that stated outright that lupus could, it was assumed that they didn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T20:49:46-08:00","id":1020157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1020133#post1020133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a>, interesting numbers, and I'm curious to know the source. Not that I don't believe, just sincerely curious. That said, it doesn't change anything else. All that you said is true, in the sense that it is the most accepted theory in lore to explain the end of the Apis. For one, it doesn't have to apply, because the Apis died for real before their animal Kin died, the Garou are still alive in this scenario. Two, the wolves didn't died, just are in the verge of (and that is in the lore already, no change), so nothing guarantees that the Lupus breed is a necessity. Three, it can be wrong, as far as anyone truly knows, since other things happened that could explain the end of the Apis. No Changing Breed, after all, that went total extinction in the past, recovered, Kin or no Kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a common theory, it's flat-out stated as the reality of the setting on the top of page 228 of W20 Changing Breeds. It does leave still-living members alive, but they become infertile. Death follows in the passing of that generation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Four, and more important, the OP wants the best way to get rid of the Lupus 'cause he doesn't like Lupus, changing the lore to accommodate for this is already a thing, there is no point in saying he's wrong and harming the lore. The lore isn't sacred, or unchangeable reality, y'now? Its just fiction. </div> </div> </div>Wave a magic wand, retcon everything. Also, lose a lot of the import of the world outside of humans that's integral to the game, but people want what they want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, and since they have alone a third of the Lupus, the Talons remain as the single main source of Lupus compared to any other tribe. &quot;Main&quot; doesn't mean &quot;responsible for more than half&quot;. </div> </div> </div>That was a rather crude ballpark on my part, and for that, I apologize. Assuming there are 14,500 non-Red Talons in the Garou Nation and all 13 tribes together are about 15,000, that makes for a bit over 2000 non-Red Talons lupus. Also, Talons tend to congregate in places deep in the wilderness where even other Garou don't, so the likelihood of finding one without some kind of funny business going on, even just among wolf-born Garou, is actually quite low.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 12-21-2016, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T22:42:37-08:00","id":1020191,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Red Talons do not want to get within sniffing distance of any human settlement. You are talking about a breed that loves Alaska, Canada, Far Eastern Russia, Mongolia, and Siberia because they do not have that many humans (though they will probably freak out over the mineral extraction and pollution). Even so, you are talking about 2,500 Lupus spread across 10 million square miles of land, meaning that the average pack of 5 Red Talons will share 20,000 square miles of the most isolated areas of the Great Wild North with their Wolf Kinfolk and Mortal Wolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T04:45:07-08:00","id":1020282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1020154#post1020154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said it wasn't a houserule. But without the books outright stating that lupus can learn languages, getting a ST to LET you have english for free was like pulling teeth. And I cannot stress how freaking common this was. There were articles all over the net how lupus were not supposed to be able to use human languages, as well.<br /> <br /> Yes it was a houserule, but it was similar to the Sleep=shift to breedform one, it was all but accepted as canon in some circles. And since the books did not have a section that stated outright that lupus could, it was assumed that they didn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know very well how those things go. Sometimes I still surprise players with &quot;house-rules that no one expected&quot;, actually the rules as written. And usually to their benefit. Its interesting, by the way, how some people conclude that if something isn't stated to follow the same rules as everyone else, it implies that somehow they are clearly exception, not just the authors saving space.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1020157#post1020157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a common theory, it's flat-out stated as the reality of the setting on the top of page 228 of W20 Changing Breeds. It does leave still-living members alive, but they become infertile. Death follows in the passing of that generation.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, first, it can happen. The Nation won't suffer noticeable effects for some years. Second, the fact that wolves still exist persist. Third, ST can change it for the chronicle.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1020157#post1020157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wave a magic wand, retcon everything. Also, lose a lot of the import of the world outside of humans that's integral to the game, but people want what they want.</div> </div> </div> </div>No magic wand, dude. Its just a game. Anyone can change anything. For lamer reasons than not wanting to think of zoophilia as a thing in the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1020157#post1020157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was a rather crude ballpark on my part, and for that, I apologize. Assuming there are 14,500 non-Red Talons in the Garou Nation and all 13 tribes together are about 15,000, that makes for a bit over 2000 non-Red Talons lupus. Also, Talons tend to congregate in places deep in the wilderness where even other Garou don't, so the likelihood of finding one without some kind of funny business going on, even just among wolf-born Garou, is actually quite low.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said it was easy to see a Talon. I said they were the major distinction in a &quot;Lupus-Free&quot; game. It stands, since the Lupus on most other tribes don't make a lot of difference <u>for</u> being Lupus.<br /> <br /> Now, as a side note and sincere question: given that a wolf gives birth with far more frequency, to more babies at once, and growing a lot faster, the game ever explained why the Garou have so much of a problem to have cubs through them? It seems so much more efficient to produce new werewolves that I can only conclude that wolves are actually far less &quot;productive&quot; in giving birth to Kin or Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T05:03:51-08:00","id":1020293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1020282#post1020282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know very well how those things go. Sometimes I still surprise players with &quot;house-rules that no one expected&quot;, actually the rules as written. And usually to their benefit. Its interesting, by the way, how some people conclude that if something isn't stated to follow the same rules as everyone else, it implies that somehow they are clearly exception, not just the authors saving space.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, with the lupus it was just the STs deciding that since lupus are born wolf, they had to be unable to function well outside being a wolf. While homids magically were able to perfectly mimic wild wolves despite never having had to use wolf body language and vocalizations before.<br /> <br /> Well, that and for a long time, lupus were just seen as distruptive or unplayable in WtA games. At times it felt like you had to have a doctor level study of wolves to play one, and even then you could get told you were not doing it right if you didn't do it exactly as the ST wanted you to.<br /> <br /> <br /> Best example of a house rule to me has to be the sleeping only in your birth form one. It came from the knock out rules and the description of the metamorph merit. Therefore, garou with the merit MUST sleep in birth form, even if there was never a rule stating it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T06:24:28-08:00","id":1020343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1020282#post1020282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, as a side note and sincere question: given that a wolf gives birth with far more frequency, to more babies at once, and growing a lot faster, the game ever explained why the Garou have so much of a problem to have cubs through them? It seems so much more efficient to produce new werewolves that I can only conclude that wolves are actually far less &quot;productive&quot; in giving birth to Kin or Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>3 reasons: The wolf population is small compared to the human population, the wolf population is shrinking, and the human population is growing. So while 100 wolf-kin, left to their own devices, could conceivably produce more Garou than 100 homid-kin, those Lupus Garou are going to be outnumbered by all the other Homid-born, and their kin are going to be hunted for sport from helicopters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T06:54:14-08:00","id":1020362,"title":"","content":"On a vaguely related note, why isn't the best course of action for the Garou to go back to killing as many humans as possible and reducing us to small, hunter-gatherer tribes. The Wrym/Weaver et. al. machinations would be severely limited without the presence of humans to implement/support their activities. And the setting seems to make it clear that there's nothing special about humans. It's not as if they're the only things that can be conscious - you can awaken a tree spirit and it will have a personality and such. Gaia doesn't even need humans to make its warriors - there were these lizard people who existed in the pre-human past (I forgot their name).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T07:15:58-08:00","id":1020384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1020362#post1020362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a vaguely related note, why isn't the best course of action for the Garou to go back to killing as many humans as possible and reducing us to small, hunter-gatherer tribes. The Wrym/Weaver et. al. machinations would be severely limited without the presence of humans to implement/support their activities. And the setting seems to make it clear that there's nothing special about humans. It's not as if they're the only things that can be conscious - you can awaken a tree spirit and it will have a personality and such. Gaia doesn't even need humans to make its warriors - there were these lizard people who existed in the pre-human past (I forgot their name).</div> </div> </div> </div>1. There are too many humans and not enough Garou. <br /> 2. There are way too many Supernatural groups that would be against that. Vampires feed off of humans so having lots of humans is good for vampires. <br /> 3. Not all Garou would be for it. Children of Gaia, Glasswalkers, maybe Bone Gnawers would be very much against it. <br /> 4. There are plenty of examples in Garou history about how Genocide is bad. War of Rage is one of them. Maybe someone with better knowledge of W:tA lore can chime in here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T07:20:23-08:00","id":1020386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1020343#post1020343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3 reasons: The wolf population is small compared to the human population, the wolf population is shrinking, and the human population is growing. So while 100 wolf-kin, left to their own devices, could conceivably produce more Garou than 100 homid-kin, those Lupus Garou are going to be outnumbered by all the other Homid-born, and their kin are going to be hunted for sport from helicopters.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I know, but am not convinced. Since Garou seem to hoard their human Kin as treasure, they could simply do the same to wolf-kin. I can't see the situation becoming so dread if they were doing this all along. Just wanted to know if there is something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T08:02:50-08:00","id":1020402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1020384#post1020384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. There are too many humans and not enough Garou.<br /> 2. There are way too many Supernatural groups that would be against that. Vampires feed off of humans so having lots of humans is good for vampires.<br /> 3. Not all Garou would be for it. Children of Gaia, Glasswalkers, maybe Bone Gnawers would be very much against it.<br /> 4. There are plenty of examples in Garou history about how Genocide is bad. War of Rage is one of them. Maybe someone with better knowledge of W:tA lore can chime in here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can agree with all of it, but it still seems like the best plan. Garou, particularly with the ability to step sideways plus delirium, could certainly spend some serious time killing/destroying every large energy/pollution production facility in a city. Yes, the're will be some temporary bad umbra juju from all of the dying humans, but in the long run Gaia will be better off. And #3 - those Garou are deluded. They like humans, but they are not human (any more than a Lupus is a wolf).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T09:35:21-08:00","id":1020442,"title":"","content":"On the &quot;why not use wolves to mass produce Garou,&quot; thing: one of the biggest problems is controlling wild wolves. Unlike human kin who will happily settle where you tell them and stay there to be family (even very large ones at that), wolves generally form fairly small packs given the amount of area one will claim. They need lots and lots of space, and even more as a kin-heavy pack starts spawning new packs (which you need to keep them functioning as wild wolf pack units since they aren't going to be able to support you getting all the females pregnant at once; assuming you even could override biology to do that). If you start caging wolves in small areas to keep them contained, safe, and accessible, you run the risk of turning them into &quot;dogs&quot; spiritually and losing their ability to have Garou pups. Also to reiterate with a bit more detail, wolves give off strong hormonal cues that actually act as a form of birth control to biologically ensure only one or two females can get pregnant in a season; so if you just have one pack of wolves kept in a sanctuary by the Sept, you're getting one or two litters of pups a year. That's... basically 1-2 Garou a year.<br /> <br /> --------------<br /> <br /> On the &quot;why not go back to culling humans,&quot; thing:<br /> <br /> Because genocide will just make the Wyrm stronger; massive slaughter does not just temporarily cause some extra banes. It can permanently alter the spiritual landscape of an area and turn it into a Blight of infinite bane-spawning grounds. Also if you're playing in the wider WoD with other supernaturals, the Technocrats will very easily stop you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T10:08:56-08:00","id":1020463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1020442#post1020442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you start caging wolves in small areas to keep them contained, safe, and accessible, you run the risk of turning them into &quot;dogs&quot; spiritually and losing their ability to have Garou pups. Also to reiterate with a bit more detail, wolves give off strong hormonal cues that actually act as a form of birth control to biologically ensure only one or two females can get pregnant in a season; so if you just have one pack of wolves kept in a sanctuary by the Sept, you're getting one or two litters of pups a year. That's... basically 1-2 Garou a year.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if (and this is a big IF) this was done in a way to avoid terrible abuse or domestication, after a few years that sept is going to be up to their eyeballs in Kin-wolves... which is sort of good, but it takes a <i>lot</i> of resources to keep dozens and dozens of wolves safe, fed, and happy. Lupus Garou breeding programs seem like obvious solutions on paper but in practice it seems borderline impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T10:12:07-08:00","id":1020464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1020384#post1020384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. There are too many humans and not enough Garou.<br /> 2. There are way too many Supernatural groups that would be against that. Vampires feed off of humans so having lots of humans is good for vampires.<br /> 3. Not all Garou would be for it. Children of Gaia, Glasswalkers, maybe Bone Gnawers would be very much against it.<br /> 4. There are plenty of examples in Garou history about how Genocide is bad. War of Rage is one of them. Maybe someone with better knowledge of W:tA lore can chime in here.</div> </div> </div> </div>These 4 reasons are a good summation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1020402#post1020402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can agree with all of it, but it still seems like the best plan. Garou, particularly with the ability to step sideways plus delirium, could certainly spend some serious time killing/destroying every large energy/pollution production facility in a city. Yes, the're will be some temporary bad umbra juju from all of the dying humans, but in the long run Gaia will be better off. And #3 - those Garou are deluded. They like humans, but they are not human (any more than a Lupus is a wolf).</div> </div> </div> </div>You would need a &quot;natural&quot; way of bringing about a mass extinction. And while afterwards, Gaia <i>might</i> be better off, you really have no way to tell. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> points out, this isn't about &quot;temporary bad umbra juju&quot;. If you cause the suffering of millions or billions of humans, the spiritual landscape will most likely never (for all intents and purposes) recover. That isn't something the Garou can afford to risk.<br /> And on your response to point #3. 80% of Garou are homid, and thus come from human stock. It isn't just those 3 Tribes that will oppose the mass extinction of the human race.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T11:01:39-08:00","id":1020501,"title":"","content":"its probaly true... but while I wont lie, I dont personally want to be &quot;Culled&quot; <br /> <br /> I find it hard to say the human race doesnt <i>Richly Deserve </i>the impergium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T11:57:00-08:00","id":1020531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1020402#post1020402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can agree with all of it, but it still seems like the best plan. Garou, particularly with the ability to step sideways plus delirium, could certainly spend some serious time killing/destroying every large energy/pollution production facility in a city. Yes, the're will be some temporary bad umbra juju from all of the dying humans, but in the long run Gaia will be better off. And #3 - those Garou are deluded. They like humans, but they are not human (any more than a Lupus is a wolf).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unless Vampires and Mages were created as an 'immune response' to the original Impergium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T12:15:15-08:00","id":1020544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1020078#post1020078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the Garou (and the Fera in general) would be much happier with 3 billion people than 7.5 billion people (though they would probably still complain about there being too many people). Of course, Kindred and KJ would be unhappy because of the lack of food.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Plenty of KJ factions that feel there are too many fucking people.. amazing how that works in the most densely populated places on the planet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T12:42:47-08:00","id":1020567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1020501#post1020501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">its probaly true... but while I wont lie, I dont personally want to be &quot;Culled&quot;<br /> <br /> I find it hard to say the human race doesnt <i>Richly Deserve </i>the impergium.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I don't want to be culled either. But the game is (apparently) about non-humans, and in the game Gaia and nature has some moral value outside of humans (i.e., if there were no humans nature would still somehow be a &quot;good&quot; thing to have), so practicalities aside, Garou should spend their time doing as much damage to humans as possible. I'm not saying it's right I'm just saying it seems to follow logically. Sorry to get us off topic, as you all answered my original question. I'm definately a much better fit for Forsaken ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T12:46:07-08:00","id":1020569,"title":"","content":"The problem would be killing enough humans quickly enough without triggering a nuclear war. Imagine the response from China if a novel pathogen starts killing off tens of millions of Chinese every month. They will suspect Russia or USA of releasing the pathogen to stop their rise to a superpower and would go to total war. The US planned response to total war with China is a full scale nuclear exchange, as there really is no other way to stop China. The Chinese counterstrike would cripple the US, the dust clouds would reduce global crop yields the following year by eighty percent, and eighty percent of humans would starve to death. That would potentially create hundreds of millions of bans and tens of millions of fomori.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T13:20:29-08:00","id":1020600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1020567#post1020567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, I don't want to be culled either. But the game is (apparently) about non-humans, and in the game Gaia and nature has some moral value outside of humans (i.e., if there were no humans nature would still somehow be a &quot;good&quot; thing to have), so practicalities aside, Garou should spend their time doing as much damage to humans as possible. I'm not saying it's right I'm just saying it seems to follow logically. Sorry to get us off topic, as you all answered my original question. I'm definately a much better fit for Forsaken ;-)</div> </div> </div> </div>So I think part of the problem with the outlook you seem to have (and by all means correct me) is that you see humans as being the sole problem in the world, according to Garou.<br /> <br /> That isn't the case. Humans have negative affects on the world in general, yes. But Garou are fighting for the soul of the world (Umbra) as much as the body (Material). Wiping out humans <i>might</i> (and that's a big might) solve one, but it would destroy the other....in most scenarios.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T13:31:29-08:00","id":1020606,"title":"","content":"In addition to that, standard Garou teachings generally portray humans as the &quot;tools&quot; or &quot;symptoms&quot; of their enemies, not their enemies directly. Wiping them out causes lots of problems, and doesn't actually defeat the enemy. It just denies both sides a useful resource. For all the damage humans do in WtA, humans don't do this because they're human. They can be taught and lead to better ways of living that empower a more Gaia-friendly spiritual influence as well. They do this because the anti-Gaian forces have out competed the Gaian forces in getting humans to behave in ways that serve other interests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T13:51:40-08:00","id":1020620,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm half-convinced on the topic of Kinfolk.<br /> <br /> That aside, I want to add two things to the topic of Impergium.<br /> <br /> First, it isn't the problem. The unbalanced is older than Humanity. The enemy is the Wyrm, maybe the Weaver. They don't need humanity to be a problem, and genocide will only serve to make matters worse on the opinions of most Garou. It isn't, indeed, an unanimous opinion, and a lot of Garou want the Impergium back for a lot of reasons, that included. But humanity, though strongly implied as making everything worse, isn't the problem. Also, we can be even a solution. The Glass Walkers are fond of recognizing human development as a next stage on natural evolution, and they can be right. Even the others find Human Kin far more useful than simple wolves, and even non-Kin can help the cause if properly educated.<br /> <br /> Second, don't overestimate the &quot;we're not humans&quot; side. Yes, they're not humans, not more than they are wolves. But they are sentient beings with feelings, and most grew-up as humans. First, it means that most still <u>see</u> themselves more as humans, as most Lupus still see themselves as wolves. A common wolf won't give a f**k if you kill a wolf that's not of its pack, but the Lupus Garou are usually very sensible with wolf suffering. They are not wolves, but as sentient beings they feel kinship with wolves. A lot of Garou feel kinship with humans. All of this also means they have personal emotion-based moral standards, as we have. Some people think the world would be better off without wolves, but a lot of completely human beings find the idea of hunting a wolf abhorrent. Most people don't like the idea of animals suffering when they don't need to, and some change habits completely to not benefit themselves from animal death or suffering in any sense. It isn't a thing we do because we're animals, its a thing we do because were sensible. Garou also are, humans or not.<br /> <br /> And third, its too late. Humanity can be individually weak, but there are reasons to fear a modern response to the Impergium. Just think of what would happen if the Pentagon found a big Caern and decided that this war went far enough. No Garou would be able to even know of the nuclear warhead fast enough, and probably it won't be the only one. A Tsar-Bomb in the vicinity of sacred places can harm the Garou to an extend very few things the Wyrm did until now can even compare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T14:51:50-08:00","id":1020662,"title":"","content":"Great points!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T17:59:52-08:00","id":1020730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1020620#post1020620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Glass Walkers are fond of recognizing human development as a next stage on natural evolution, and they can be right.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of people do, but they're stone cold wrong in this context, because they're crowbarring something into a biological discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T07:28:09-08:00","id":1020871,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a>, given modern academic discussions and theories on both Human and Biological sciences, your assertive can only be considered undisputed truth in the limited context of a specific fictional or dogmatic canon.<br /> <br /> Further, given the &quot;unreliable narrator&quot; nature of most text on the setting, namely that they are usually presented in the context of a given group's world-view, I should add that in this case it is just your headcanon.<br /> <br /> Not that it isn't a popular take on the subject, it is, but it still isn't such a given. There is no proof that any particular Tribe or Breed is wrong in its theories, and none of them agree on so much details. IC, the fault of humanity is a very popular thought, but at no point put OoC as beyond doubt.<br /> <br /> There is nothing wrong with personally agreeing with the characters on any subject, but you seem too much on a rush to assert the correctness of the Nation's viewpoints.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T12:36:21-08:00","id":1020973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1020871#post1020871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a>, given modern academic discussions and theories on both Human and Biological sciences, your assertive can only be considered undisputed truth in the limited context of a specific fictional or dogmatic canon.<br /> <br /> Further, given the &quot;unreliable narrator&quot; nature of most text on the setting, namely that they are usually presented in the context of a given group's world-view, I should add that in this case it is just your headcanon.<br /> <br /> Not that it isn't a popular take on the subject, it is, but it still isn't such a given. There is no proof that any particular Tribe or Breed is wrong in its theories, and none of them agree on so much details. IC, the fault of humanity is a very popular thought, but at no point put OoC as beyond doubt.<br /> <br /> There is nothing wrong with personally agreeing with the characters on any subject, but you seem too much on a rush to assert the correctness of the Nation's viewpoints.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, when someone is declaring a given event that has serious consequences as &quot;evolution&quot;, they're trying to make peace with something terrible that's happened to a big part of the world and declaring that they don't want to think about what the world was like beforehand anymore. It's a classic dodge in the social Darwinism playbook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T13:51:13-08:00","id":1020993,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a>, I don't know why you quoted me, given that you didn't answered anything I said. You could simply use an @.<br /> <br /> Yes, the use of &quot;evolution&quot; can be just a way to make peace with the past. I don't know why non-human creatures that try to save nature anyway would try to &quot;make peace&quot; with a failure that isn't theirs, though. Maybe they truly have reasons to think that way. Maybe they are only trying to give an excuse to embrace technological advance.<br /> <br /> By the way, most people who regard the past as sacred, and the present as spoiled by other people are just unable to cope with change. Religious zealots do it a lot, regarding &quot;their time&quot; as so more pure and good, when it was actually as sick as the present or even worse. And as far as I remember, most Garou are religious zealots, right to the terrorist level. Some people don't want to think through it, so they whine about the ugly present and its damn changes, and try to force the world through violence to keep it as they want.<br /> <br /> Its an even <u>older</u> classic in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T14:25:58-08:00","id":1021005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1020993#post1020993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a>, I don't know why you quoted me, given that you didn't answered anything I said. You could simply use an @.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm confused about your objections to using the quote feature, because it's been a forum standard to responding to someone for ages and I see no reason to pick up on @someone's name. Or are we getting meta, here?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, the use of &quot;evolution&quot; can be just a way to make peace with the past. I don't know why non-human creatures that try to save nature anyway would try to &quot;make peace&quot; with a failure that isn't theirs, though. </div> </div> </div>Inevitably, just about any failure to do anything positive in Werewolf is the Garou's failure, until and unless a book comes out to reveal a bigger failure on the part of the Mokole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe they truly have reasons to think that way. Maybe they are only trying to give an excuse to embrace technological advance. </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's basically what's happening. Glass Walkers are very comfortable with human cultural norms, to the point where the culture of other Garou begins to rankle them slightly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By the way, most people who regard the past as sacred, and the present as spoiled by other people are just unable to cope with change. Religious zealots do it a lot, regarding &quot;their time&quot; as so more pure and good, when it was actually as sick as the present or even worse. And as far as I remember, most Garou are religious zealots </div> </div> </div>Except that the setting is constructed so that they actually aren't zealots any more than the characters in any given work of guarding against supernatural danger that is real and defies their beliefs. Because it doesn't take believing in banes, fomori, or the like for them to be a threat in Werewolf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> , right to the terrorist level. </div> </div> </div>That's a very modern frame on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some people don't want to think through it, so they whine about the ugly present and its damn changes, and try to force the world through violence to keep it as they want.<br /> <br /> Its an even <u>older</u> classic in the book. </div> </div> </div>Social Darwinism is another type of the same, but it's an acknowledged specific manifestation of it with acknowledged mis-use of particular words. Hence, the objection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T15:02:34-08:00","id":1021025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1021005#post1021005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm confused about your objections to using the quote feature, because it's been a forum standard to responding to someone for ages and I see no reason to pick up on @someone's name. Or are we getting meta, here?</div> </div> </div> </div>The previous question wasn't an objection, just a statement that you ignored everything I said in the quoted part. Also, the @someone's name have the same effect when you have no need for the quote, or otherwise finds the quote inappropriate. I had also some problems to get used to it, but now I find it very useful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1021005#post1021005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inevitably, just about any failure to do anything positive in Werewolf is the Garou's failure, until and unless a book comes out to reveal a bigger failure on the part of the Mokole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without a doubt, indeed. But it doesn't makes the GW more failed, or failing in that particular aspect. It always seemed to me more of a failure the resolution on the Garou of being ignorant and distant from human society, mining their efforts by keeping them from better understand the context of their fight. They have a good grasp of an aspect, are blind to the other. And the GW are so alone out there that no one can keep them from doing s**t with their position.<br /> <br /> Question is, &quot;humans are of the Weaver and shitted on the world&quot; isn't a GW failure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1021005#post1021005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that's basically what's happening. Glass Walkers are very comfortable with human cultural norms, to the point where the culture of other Garou begins to rankle them slightly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, they're going precisely that direction. I'm not saying they are not. But it doesn't mean their reasoning is so completely wrong. Nothing in the game says it, except the opinions of equally deluded people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1021005#post1021005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that the setting is constructed so that they actually aren't zealots any more than the characters in any given work of guarding against supernatural danger that is real and defies their beliefs. Because it doesn't take believing in banes, fomori, or the like for them to be a threat in Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, they surely are! Yes, Banes, Fomori, BSD, and much more do exist. The setting makes it very clear that a lot of bad supernatural things do exist. But the Garou Nation isn't about skeptics that act over observed threats from a purely practical perspective. They have a complex system of meaning and mythology. And a lot of things they do aren't just reactions to demonstrable threats, but very active interventions based on belief. So much that they don't even agree among themselves on a lot of this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1021005#post1021005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a very modern frame on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, its a modern word for an ancient phenomena. The point being, Garou take their perceived duties to violent extremes, as much as they do actual threats, if not even more. And they are very indiscriminate with this violence. The word used to ascribe it isn't relevant. And since they live in a modern setting, I see no reason whatsoever to think they can't be analyzed by modern standards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1021005#post1021005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Social Darwinism is another type of the same, but it's an acknowledged specific manifestation of it with acknowledged mis-use of particular words. Hence, the objection.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I got it, you're saying that the use of the word &quot;evolution&quot; specifically instantly means not wanting to think about the past. Is that so?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T21:15:58-08:00","id":1021134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1021025#post1021025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The previous question wasn't an objection, just a statement that you ignored everything I said in the quoted part. Also, the @someone's name have the same effect when you have no need for the quote, or otherwise finds the quote inappropriate. I had also some problems to get used to it, but now I find it very useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may be too late to say it, but your initial reply didn't exactly make a lot of sense to my original frame of context, either. I was clarifying myself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Without a doubt, indeed. But it doesn't makes the GW more failed, or failing in that particular aspect. It always seemed to me more of a failure the resolution on the Garou of being ignorant and distant from human society, mining their efforts by keeping them from better understand the context of their fight. They have a good grasp of an aspect, are blind to the other. And the GW are so alone out there that no one can keep them from doing s**t with their position. </div> </div> </div>Not quite. It's because they didn't take action when they should have and took other actions when they should have kept away from the field. In that, the Glass Walkers are still culpable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Question is, &quot;humans are of the Weaver and shitted on the world&quot; isn't a GW failure. </div> </div> </div>That's not a question. And yes, it still is, in part. Because they're Garou, and their totem only rose to prominence with the vast amount of material waste of humanity and the towering edifices that produce it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, they're going precisely that direction. I'm not saying they are not. But it doesn't mean their reasoning is so completely wrong. Nothing in the game says it, except the opinions of equally deluded people. </div> </div> </div>They are often too accepting of what gets built on the land they once... (sunglasses) Warded.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, they surely are! Yes, Banes, Fomori, BSD, and much more do exist. The setting makes it very clear that a lot of bad supernatural things do exist. But the Garou Nation isn't about skeptics that act over observed threats from a purely practical perspective. They have a complex system of meaning and mythology. And a lot of things they do aren't just reactions to demonstrable threats, but very active interventions based on belief. So much that they don't even agree among themselves on a lot of this. </div> </div> </div>Nope. Chiminage is a system of payments and services, occasionally predicated on mythology but never requiring that you believe anything. There's nothing keeping it from being a purely practical arrangement from the standpoint of most werewolves, even with Rage. Reverence to Gaia can also be handled in the sense of Gaia being the feeling of health and rightness within and without, and Rage being fury over the creeping malaise of illness and corruption. It gets very visceral for Garou and Fera before it gets religious.<br /> <br /> Also, it'd be difficult to be skeptics given the long history of the Garou and Fera with the spirit world. It's something they kept when humanity shut it out. There's discovery to be had, but a lot of it is in discovering what you broke and trying to fix it. And there's probably always room to find out another thing that needs fixing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, its a modern word for an ancient phenomena. The point being, Garou take their perceived duties to violent extremes, as much as they do actual threats, if not even more. And they are very indiscriminate with this violence. The word used to ascribe it isn't relevant. And since they live in a modern setting, I see no reason whatsoever to think they can't be analyzed by modern standards. </div> </div> </div>There's still a rather large part of the setting that involves venturing into the Umbra - which is explicitly described as more real than the physical world, where killing the spirit has more impact than killing the flesh - and defeating threats there. That really doesn't fit in those bounds, even if it causes the ruination and breakdown of something important to humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I got it, you're saying that the use of the word &quot;evolution&quot; specifically instantly means not wanting to think about the past. Is that so? </div> </div> </div>In the context of someone saying something like &quot;it's evolution that we did something terrible to you and you're going to die, just accept it&quot;, yes. It's a statement of apathy from someone who can just sit back and relax while you're likely expiring.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T07:04:09-08:00","id":1021259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1021134#post1021134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It may be too late to say it, but your initial reply didn't exactly make a lot of sense to my original frame of context, either. I was clarifying myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, ok. Sorry, then.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1021134#post1021134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not quite. It's because they didn't take action when they should have and took other actions when they should have kept away from the field. In that, the Glass Walkers are still culpable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if I get you or if I made me clear here... I mean, three points: Point 1, Walkers are as culpable as everyone else, including having taken part on both the Impergium and the decision to cease it. Point 2, the game lets it open if the greater error was to start the Impergium or to stop it, and to what degree. Point 3, the game makes it clear that most tribes are anachronistic, they go to some effort to keep themselves separated from the modern world, and because of that have a hard time grasping it, doesn't matter if they accept it or not. So, the only thing here you can argue is that the GW are more prone to a side of the question, as the Talons are prone to the opposite.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1021134#post1021134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not a question. And yes, it still is, in part. Because they're Garou, and their totem only rose to prominence with the vast amount of material waste of humanity and the towering edifices that produce it.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, cockroaches live pretty fine in the wild, and their presence in wild terrain didn't diminished with their presence in the city. But this have nothing to do with it. The GW didn't caused the human behavior or dominion over the natural world more than any other werewolf. They voiced for the end of the Impergium, but that's all, they were not alone in this nor had taken the final word on the matter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1021134#post1021134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are often too accepting of what gets built on the land they once... (sunglasses) Warded.</div> </div> </div> </div>They didn't warded land, to begin with, they warded people, there is a difference. And every other tribe fall in the same, they get too accepting of something related to their role, including things they shouldn't. Again, I'm not saying the GW aren't in fault, I'm saying everyone is. On top of that, it means that other tribes can't be taken as unavoidably more right about things than the GW, so they just deserve as much doubt as everyone else.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1021134#post1021134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. Chiminage is a system of payments and services, occasionally predicated on mythology but never requiring that you believe anything. There's nothing keeping it from being a purely practical arrangement from the standpoint of most werewolves, even with Rage. Reverence to Gaia can also be handled in the sense of Gaia being the feeling of health and rightness within and without, and Rage being fury over the creeping malaise of illness and corruption. It gets very visceral for Garou and Fera before it gets religious.<br /> <br /> Also, it'd be difficult to be skeptics given the long history of the Garou and Fera with the spirit world. It's something they kept when humanity shut it out. There's discovery to be had, but a lot of it is in discovering what you broke and trying to fix it. And there's probably always room to find out another thing that needs fixing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rage isn't fury over malaise and corruption. Rage just is. Fixing things is a question of belief and perspective, because fix is to make something that is wrong into a right, and you can't do that without defining what is right and what is wrong. It IS subjective, by definition, until you have a clear arbitrary definition to make things objective in the context of a subjective paradigm. Having a reason to not be a skeptic still means you're not a skeptic. It is visceral, yes, the game does have it a strong theme. But it doesn't preclude being religious.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1021134#post1021134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's still a rather large part of the setting that involves venturing into the Umbra - which is explicitly described as more real than the physical world, where killing the spirit has more impact than killing the flesh - and defeating threats there. That really doesn't fit in those bounds, even if it causes the ruination and breakdown of something important to humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>And in what it makes the Garou less of a bunch of self-righteous maniacs that assume responsibility for things beyond their own lives and take the matter in their own claws with homicidal violence?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1021134#post1021134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the context of someone saying something like &quot;it's evolution that we did something terrible to you and you're going to die, just accept it&quot;, yes. It's a statement of apathy from someone who can just sit back and relax while you're likely expiring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's a relief that the GW didn't make such a thing, so, isn't it? Because they go as far as any other Garou to protect Gaia, to fend off the Wyrm, to be sure that wild life still exists, etcetera, etcetera, and so on and so forth. They didn't created cities, either. They just think that cities aren't the problem, and can exist in harmony with Gaia. Not that they do not house a lot of problems right now, mind you. But that they are a step in the way of the world, as many other steps before.<br /> <br /> Of course, there are several reasons to think it is a delusion, like species being killed, that happened way before cities. And species having to adapt to a hard and poisonous ambient, like the crate of a volcano and several other that happens in nature. And a single species changing the world around, definitely something not done before by a huge lot of animals. Or a species that destroys others for their own sake, of course, even plants do that in the nature, but that's another thing completely, sure.<br /> <br /> Nature isn't pretty. Animals die. A true wolf don't care if you murder every other wolf outside its pack and future mate. If they could, they would do it themselves, to get rid of competition. I'm just trying to say that there are no reason to take &quot;the GW stance is wrong&quot; for granted. YOU can believe that, in the context of the game or outside it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T13:46:36-08:00","id":1021388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019815-what-happens-if-no-lupus?p=1021259#post1021259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure if I get you or if I made me clear here... I mean, three points: Point 1, Walkers are as culpable as everyone else, including having taken part on both the Impergium and the decision to cease it. Point 2, the game lets it open if the greater error was to start the Impergium or to stop it, and to what degree. Point 3, the game makes it clear that most tribes are anachronistic, they go to some effort to keep themselves separated from the modern world, and because of that have a hard time grasping it, doesn't matter if they accept it or not. So, the only thing here you can argue is that the GW are more prone to a side of the question, as the Talons are prone to the opposite.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is less about the Impergium and far more about what came after. The Glass Walkers stuck around their cities and abetted their spread, because they have allies in the city and they're beholden to certain types of urban spirits for support, who tend to skew their territory concerns toward &quot;more urban land is better&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First, cockroaches live pretty fine in the wild, and their presence in wild terrain didn't diminished with their presence in the city. But this have nothing to do with it. The GW didn't caused the human behavior or dominion over the natural world more than any other werewolf. They voiced for the end of the Impergium, but that's all, they were not alone in this nor had taken the final word on the matter. </div> </div> </div>They haven't managed to curb it, either. Which they've had a lot of time to try doing, but they didn't see the threat on the horizon, and only ended up living in the mess and telling everyone it was actually great. Also, if cities crumbled down to nothing, there would be way, way fewer cockroaches, rats, and other animals that really manage to exploit living in close proximity to humans very well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They didn't warded land, to begin with, they warded people, there is a difference. </div> </div> </div>The original name of the tribe, when it formed, was the Warders of the Land.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And every other tribe fall in the same, they get too accepting of something related to their role, including things they shouldn't. Again, I'm not saying the GW aren't in fault, I'm saying everyone is. On top of that, it means that other tribes can't be taken as unavoidably more right about things than the GW, so they just deserve as much doubt as everyone else. </div> </div> </div>They're still the danger of cutting too much away to continue living in a new normal for them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rage isn't fury over malaise and corruption. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>W20 p144</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Every Garou is a crucible for Gaia's primal anger - her Rage at the pillage of the world at the hands of the Weaver and Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the text goes back and forth on this, Rage is quite often described as fury over corruption and ruination. And those things can contribute to a steady increase of Rage over the normal limit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rage just is. Fixing things is a question of belief and perspective, because fix is to make something that is wrong into a right, and you can't do that without defining what is right and what is wrong. It IS subjective, by definition, until you have a clear arbitrary definition to make things objective in the context of a subjective paradigm. Having a reason to not be a skeptic still means you're not a skeptic. It is visceral, yes, the game does have it a strong theme. But it doesn't preclude being religious. </div> </div> </div>The Werewolf Revised Storyteller's Handbook has a lot to say about that on page 36, and while it doesn't preclude religion, it makes no bones about religion being something very different from the experience of being Garou or Fera. It opens with a quote, &quot;All Garou are spiritual. Not all of us are religious.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And in what it makes the Garou less of a bunch of self-righteous maniacs that assume responsibility for things beyond their own lives and take the matter in their own claws with homicidal violence? </div> </div> </div>It's like complaining about someone striking back at you when you've burned down their house, killed their family, and stabbed them, in some respects. Or even that you've just taken something after all of that happened; you might think it's small, but to a Changer, it's the latest in a long list of wrongs. That, of course, cannot change that violence is violence, but the significance of what came before cannot be ignored.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, that's a relief that the GW didn't make such a thing, so, isn't it? Because they go as far as any other Garou to protect Gaia, to fend off the Wyrm, to be sure that wild life still exists, etcetera, etcetera, and so on and so forth. They didn't created cities, either. They just think that cities aren't the problem, and can exist in harmony with Gaia. Not that they do not house a lot of problems right now, mind you. But that they are a step in the way of the world, as many other steps before.<br /> <br /> Of course, there are several reasons to think it is a delusion, like species being killed, that happened way before cities. </div> </div> </div>Unlike then, there's a face to the cause, and the certain knowledge that it chose to ruin everything to make for an easy life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And species having to adapt to a hard and poisonous ambient, like the crate of a volcano and several other that happens in nature. And a single species changing the world around, definitely something not done before by a huge lot of animals. Or a species that destroys others for their own sake, of course, even plants do that in the nature, but that's another thing completely, sure.<br /> <br /> Nature isn't pretty. Animals die. A true wolf don't care if you murder every other wolf outside its pack and future mate. If they could, they would do it themselves, to get rid of competition. I'm just trying to say that there are no reason to take &quot;the GW stance is wrong&quot; for granted. YOU can believe that, in the context of the game or outside it. </div> </div> </div>Tu quoque.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T01:00:50-08:00","id":1021492,"title":"","content":"Ok, I got you, I think. Still disagree, but since we managed to almost take over the thread in a mostly unrelated discussion, and it doesn't seem to be going anywhere, I see no point in furthering this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}